{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Thus.</b> And formed you from the womb — an allusion to Jacob, in the sense of בבטן עקב את אחיו (in the womb he supplanted his brother) (Hosea 12:4), and there I will explain it. Or it is by way of metaphor, and from the womb means from the day they became a people for a name:" "<b>Jeshurun.</b> From the root ישר (upright), and it is an epithet of the Name, and its pattern is like אפס."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:52.033500789Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}